From plessy at debian.org  Fri Oct  4 00:47:23 2024
From: plessy at debian.org (Charles Plessy)
Date: Fri, 4 Oct 2024 09:47:23 +0900
Subject: Too mamy wishlist bugs
Message-ID: <Zv87G34cyyXWTOez@kumo.plessy.net>

Hi Ben,

I appreciate your interest to contribute, but I think that opening many
wishlist bugs for one-line changes is counter-productive.  Please
consider the time it takes managing these bugs, compared with the time
it takes maning the one-line change.

For instance, if we want to standardise the homepage field to point to
CRAN, we can modify our routine-update script the change will be done
automatically at each new upload.

Another way to contribute small changes is to make merge requests on
Salsa.  I think that a few clicks are less time-consuming than copying
or cut-pasting many 6-digits bug numbers plenty of times.

So please before mass-filing bugs consult with us.

Have a nice day,

Charles

